in E1? No, E1 is inside the class. I'll add a separate edit anchored at `_FORMAT = \"[%(levelname)s...` line: replace\n```\n_FORMAT = \"[%(levelname)s %(asctime)s %(filename)s:%(lineno)d] %(message)s\"\n_DATE_FORMAT = \"%m-%d %H:%M:%S\"\n```\nwith those plus marker/helper. Good, that's a unique anchor.\n\nE3: replace format method body to insert truncation via copy record.\n\nOriginal format:\n```python\n    def format(self, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str:\n        msg = super().format(record)\n        # 快速路径：单行日志（绝大多数情况）无需做对齐处理\n        if \"\\n\" in msg and record.message:\n            prefix = msg[: msg.find(record.message)]\n            msg = msg.replace(\"\\n\", \"\\n\" + prefix)\n        if self.use_color:\n            color = _LEVEL_COLORS.get(record.levelno)\n            if color:\n                msg = f\"{color}{msg}{_COLOR_RESET}\"\n        return msg\n```\nNew:\n```python\n    def format(self, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str:\n        if self.max_message_chars is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True:\n            message = record.getMessage()\n            truncated = self._truncate_message(message)\n            if truncated != message:\n                record = logging.makeLogRecord(dict(record.__dict__))\n                record.msg = truncated\n                record.args = ()\n        msg = super().format(record)\n        ...\n```\nCareful: `makeLogRecord` copies __dict__ incl. exc_info/stack_info/levelno etc. It sets .message maybe. Fine.\n\nNote: the copy's `record.message` will be recomputed by Formatter.format. Good.\n\nAlso the copy retains `keep_full_message` attr; irrelevant.\n\nHmm one issue: `logging.makeLogRecord(dict(record.__dict__))` — makeLogRecord(dict) creates LogRecord(None, None, \"\", 0, \"\", (), None, None) then __dict__.update(dict). That copies everything, including 'message' if present. Fine.\n\nE4: _setup_logger fmt creation → pass max_message_chars from config.\n\nNow environ: what about \