       if self.max_message_chars is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True:\n            rendered = record.getMessage()\n            truncated = self._truncate_message(rendered)\n            if truncated != rendered:\n                # 复制一份记录再截断，绝不改写共享 LogRecord 的 msg/args 等字段\n                record = logging.makeLogRecord(dict(record.__dict__))\n                record.msg = truncated\n                record.args = ()\n        msg = super().format(record)\n        ...rest same...\n```\n\nNote: for tail, `message[len(message)-tail:]`; if tail==0 → message[len:] = \"\" fine.\n\nNow let me write everything and run pytest at the end.\n\nAlso need run.log/patch.diff. I'll handle in next turn (check).\n\nLet me produce the block now.\n\nOne risk: stats_logger's `_log_worker` line indentation exactly 16 spaces for `logger.info(m)`. From evidence:\n```\n            for m in msgs:\n                logger.info(m)\n```\n16 spaces before logger. Good.\n\nRun pytest after edits.\n\nAlso print `python -m pytest -q` rc.\n\nWrite code."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9257,"completion_tokens":8584,"total_tokens":17841,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":4096},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":8477},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":4096,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":5161},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}